---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = "Rabbia Ashraf Attains International Accreditation as Certified ADOS-2 Clinical Practitioner";
const description = "Clinical Child Psychologist Rabbia Ashraf achieves certified practitioner credentials in the ADOS-2 (Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule, Second Edition), setting a benchmark for gold-standard autism evaluation and clinical fidelity.";
const canonicalURL = "https://www.rabbiapsychologist.com/press/rabbia-ashraf-certified-ados-2-practitioner-autism-assessment/";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalURL={canonicalURL}>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 max-w-3xl bg-white shadow-sm rounded-xl my-12 border border-gray-100">
    <article>
      <header class="mb-8 border-b border-gray-100 pb-6">
        <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 bg-brand-sky/20 text-brand-navy text-xs font-semibold rounded-full mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">
          Official Press Release
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4 leading-tight">
          Rabbia Ashraf Attains International Accreditation as Certified ADOS-2 Clinical Practitioner
        </h1>
        <h2 class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-4 font-normal leading-relaxed">
          The milestone credential reinforces Rabbia Psychologist Child Development Services as a regional and international center of clinical excellence for gold-standard autism observational assessment.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide">
          <time datetime="2026-10-18">October 18, 2026</time> • Lahore / Global
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>LAHORE & GLOBAL</strong> — Rabbia Psychologist Child Development Services today announced that its founder and principal clinical psychologist, <strong>Rabbia Ashraf</strong>, has achieved international certification as an <strong>ADOS-2 (Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule, Second Edition) Certified Clinical Practitioner</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          The ADOS-2 is globally recognized by pediatricians, clinical psychologists, and researchers as the clinical gold standard for observational assessment of Autism Spectrum Conditions across ages, developmental stages, and expressive language levels. Achieving certified practitioner status represents an advanced level of diagnostic fidelity, clinical observation skill, and inter-rater reliability.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-brand-trust pl-4 italic text-gray-800 text-lg my-6 bg-brand-cream/60 p-5 rounded-r-lg">
          “An autism assessment should never be a tick-box exercise or an intimidating barrier for parents. Accurate, neurodiversity-affirming, and clinically rigorous observation with the ADOS-2 gives families a compassionate blueprint of how their child communicates, interacts, and perceives the world. Achieving certified practitioner accreditation allows us to evaluate children with unmatched fidelity and give parents clear, actionable roadmaps.”
          <footer class="mt-2 text-sm not-italic font-semibold text-brand-navy">— Rabbia Ashraf, Clinical Child Psychologist & Certified ADOS-2 Practitioner</footer>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mt-8 mb-3">Raising the Standard for Autism Evaluation & Assessment</h3>
        <p>
          With neurodevelopmental concerns rising globally and waiting lists often stretching up to 18 to 24 months, many families encounter inconsistent assessment quality, misinterpretations, or reports filled with incomprehensible jargon.
        </p>

        <p>
          As a Certified ADOS-2 Practitioner, Rabbia Ashraf provides specialized clinical services including:
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Gold-Standard Clinical Evaluation:</strong> Precise administration of ADOS-2 Modules across toddlers, non-verbal children, fluent adolescents, and nuanced presentations in girls and intellectually gifted youth.</li>
          <li><strong>Inter-Rater Reliability & Diagnostic Fidelity:</strong> Standardized coding of behavioral presses that eliminates subjective bias and aligns with international multidisciplinary protocols.</li>
          <li><strong>Translation for Families & Schools:</strong> Bridging the gap between dense diagnostic scores and actionable Individualized Education Programs (IEPs), sensory accommodations, and parent co-regulation strategies at home.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 text-sm mt-8 rounded-xl space-y-2">
          <strong class="text-brand-navy block">Clinical Practice & Scope Note:</strong>
          <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">
            Rabbia Psychologist Child Development Services provides specialized clinical assessment, parent guidance, and developmental consultations. Formal diagnostic determinations are conducted in accordance with international ethical standards and multidisciplinary protocols. Online international consultations provide parent guidance, psychoeducation, and report review, complementing local medical and crisis care pathways.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-navy text-white rounded-xl flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1">Book an Autism Assessment Consultation</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm m-0">Inquire about ADOS-2 clinical assessments, developmental evaluations, or parent report reviews.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/book/" class="inline-block bg-brand-trust text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-bold hover:bg-blue-600 transition-colors shrink-0 shadow-md">
            Schedule Consultation
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <p><strong>Media & Clinical Inquiries:</strong><br />
        Rabbia Ashraf, Clinical Psychologist<br />
        Rabbia Psychologist Child Development Services<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:psychologistrabbia@gmail.com" class="text-brand-trust underline">psychologistrabbia@gmail.com</a><br />
        Website: <a href="https://www.rabbiapsychologist.com" class="text-brand-trust underline">www.rabbiapsychologist.com</a></p>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "NewsArticle",
    "headline": "Rabbia Ashraf Attains International Accreditation as Certified ADOS-2 Clinical Practitioner",
    "description": description,
    "datePublished": "2026-10-18T18:00:00+05:00",
    "dateModified": "2026-10-18T20:00:00+05:00",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Rabbia Ashraf",
      "jobTitle": "Clinical Psychologist & Certified ADOS-2 Practitioner",
      "url": "https://www.rabbiapsychologist.com/about/"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Rabbia Psychologist Child Development Services",
      "url": "https://www.rabbiapsychologist.com"
    },
    "mainEntityOfPage": canonicalURL
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
